CAVEAT:  Two things are NOT MEASURED by this case, on purpose.  Neither was improvised.
         1. CONFIGURATION APPLIED FROM A FILE while the device operates
            (`copy <file> running-config`, `activate <script>.scp`).  NOT MEASURED.  It
            needs a `.scp` or configuration file on the DUT's flash.  Putting one there
            needs a root write to the testbox's `/tftproot`, which is the Test Engineer's
            to do (STANDING-ORDERS section 4).  This is a bench limit, not a product
            limit.
         2. A CHANGE MEASURED MID-FLOW, as a number of frames lost at the instant of the
            change.  NOT MEASURED as a timing number.  Every step below measures the
            state BEFORE and the state AFTER with counted bursts.  That proves THAT the
            change took effect while the device was running, and it bounds WHEN to the
            few seconds between the `end` command and the next leg's first frame.  A
            figure below one second would need a continuous rate-limited stream that
            spans the configuration command.  No tool in `tools/` drives such a stream
            from the same process as a console write.  The bound is stated; no precision
            is claimed.
