STEP 3 -- CHANGE: the bound filter is edited in place and the two flows swap state PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Method: this is the strongest form of the test.  It is not "remove, then add again".
  It is a change to a filter that is bound to a live port right now, with two flows that
  must exchange their fates.

awplus(config)#access-list hardware ckdyn
  % This access-list is attached to an interface. The modified configuration will be applied to the interface automatically after exiting this configuration mode  by entering "exit" or "end" command.
awplus(config-ip-hw-acl)#no deny tcp any any eq 22
awplus(config-ip-hw-acl)#deny icmp any any
awplus(config-ip-hw-acl)#end

  <-- That `% ` line is ADVICE, not a rejection.  This platform has two near-identical
      messages whose difference is one word: `is attached` is advice, `is currently
      attached` is a rejection.  `tools/cfg.py` carried on correctly because the string
      is in its advisory list.  Had the tool treated it as an error, this step would have
      read as a product failure while the product was working.  The message also says
      WHEN the change lands: not at the rule, but on leaving the sub-mode.

awplus#show access-list                       [read 7 s later]
  Hardware IP access list ckdyn
      4 deny icmp any any

