STEP 7 -- a change made dynamically is saved and survives a restart               PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Method: apply the STEP 5a change again, save it, reload the DUT, and read the same
  signatures before anyone logs in.  One leg sends ICMP to BOTH addresses, so each leg
  carries its own control: whichever address is the subject, the other must NOT answer,
  and the source address of the unreachable says which one the DUT currently holds.

tb277# sudo arpleg.py --tag <tag> --out /tmp/ntp1021/T47192 --iface eth4 \
       --icmp 10.38.22.66,10.38.22.70 --sender-ip 10.38.22.65 \
       --sender-mac 00:0d:b9:55:77:0f --gw-mac e0:1a:ea:d4:70:43 --count 4 --wait 4

  Baseline, vlan48 is .66:
  cap t192-base-eth4.pcap: 19 frame(s)
